cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the paper and the archived repository."
title: "Code and data for: Pharmacological efficacy is an emergent property of a receptor-wide allosteric network"
abstract: >-
  Code and input data reproducing every figure in a deep mutational
  pharmacology study of the human mu-opioid receptor (OPRM1), in which
  approximately 400,000 measurements of variant effects on signalling and
  surface expression were collected across 15 opioid ligands, including
  concentration-response scans for morphine, fentanyl and DAMGO.
type: dataset
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthewkarlhoward/HaloTag-MOR_DMS"
keywords:
  - deep mutational scanning
  - GPCR
  - mu-opioid receptor
  - OPRM1
  - allostery
  - pharmacological efficacy
  - opioids
